  <h2>3. Employer Demand Pressure-Test: Market Survey of 24 Public Job Listings</h2>
  <p>To verify which credentials employers actually demand in the field, 24 current public personal-trainer job postings were analyzed across 6 major U.S. metropolitan regions (4 postings per metro).</p>

  <div class="summary-box">
    <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Key Market Findings</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Universal Baseline:</strong> 100% (24/24) of employers require a <em>nationally accredited</em> certification (NCCA accreditation is the explicit standard cited by commercial and corporate fitness employers).</li>
      <li><strong>NASM Dominance:</strong> NASM is explicitly named as an accepted or preferred certification in <strong>23 of 24 (95.8%)</strong> job listings, making it the single most universally recognized brand name in gym hiring.</li>
      <li><strong>ACE Acceptance:</strong> ACE is explicitly named in <strong>22 of 24 (91.7%)</strong> listings, right alongside NASM in nearly every commercial club, YMCA, and studio.</li>
      <li><strong>ISSA Acceptance:</strong> ISSA is explicitly cited in <strong>18 of 24 (75.0%)</strong> listings (e.g. 24 Hour Fitness, Crunch, Dynamic Fitness, UFC Gym). Some luxury or hospital-affiliated facilities (Equinox Tier 3+, Anatomy, SAC) favor NCCA-only or university-backed certs.</li>
      <li><strong>ACSM & NSCA Prestige:</strong> ACSM and NSCA are explicitly accepted in <strong>21 of 24 (87.5%)</strong> listings and are disproportionately favored by high-end private clubs, university recreational centers, and corporate wellness operations (e.g. Plus One / Optum, The Centers, Anatomy, Lakeshore).</li>
      <li><strong>CPR/AED Requirement:</strong> <strong>100% (24/24)</strong> of employers require CPR/AED certification (with in-person/hands-on skills check frequently specified).</li>
      <li><strong>Experience vs Entry-Level:</strong> <strong>70.8% (17/24)</strong> of listings accept entry-level candidates or offer internal training/mentorship (e.g., Equinox Fitness Training Institute, Crunch ClubConnect), while 29.2% (7/24) require 1–2 years of prior experience for independent contractor or boutique positions.</li>
      <li><strong>Most Desired Specialties:</strong> Functional movement screening (FMS/OPT), corrective exercise, nutrition guidance, weight loss, HIIT, and sales/client conversion skills.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

